,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5571127827","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121641#issuecomment-5571127827","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121641","id":5571127827,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTBCqEw","user":{"login":"chokomancarr","id":6769909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Njk5MDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6769909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chokomancarr","html_url":"https://github.com/chokomancarr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chokomancarr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chokomancarr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chokomancarr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chokomancarr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chokomancarr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chokomancarr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chokomancarr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chokomancarr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chokomancarr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-07T13:10:14Z","updated_at":"2026-09-07T13:10:14Z","body":"I am not particularly familiar with the rest of the engine, but...\r\n\r\n    lazily allocating the command buffer when it's requested\r\n\r\nBased on a quick search, perhaps that can be done by doing the cmd buffer initialization in `_multimesh_get_command_buffer_rd_rid`? since that must be called by user to fill in the data, and called by the renderer as well. However, `_multimesh_set_mesh` has to conditionally free / update the cmd buffer anyway if the new mesh has different surface / vertex counts.\r\n\r\nPersonally i would just let it allocate twice si